    {
      "id": "MO-DEC-01",
      "decision": "FIX",
      "rationale": "Default official OAuth credential callback must reuse current runtime attempt getter, including cleanup. Preserve errors/backend; no replacement retry or retained cleanup credential."
    },
    {
      "id": "MO-DEC-02",
      "decision": "FIX",
      "rationale": "Official changed callback and existing observer share runtime currentness forwarding helper; preserve exact official marker and no completion argument versus legacy completion forwarding."
    },
    {
      "id": "MO-DEC-03",
      "decision": "FIX",
      "rationale": "Reuse official disposed latch after awaited scope and immediately before write; same-account stale writes refuse, admitted I/O retains outcome without replay or synthetic cancellation."
    },
    {
      "id": "MO-DEC-04",
      "decision": "ADOPT",
      "rationale": "Minimal thin resource-bridge repair only; existing official business policy and full Rust migration remain open. Real default-composition controls in existing whole-file selected suite, no new workflow or test runtime."
    },
    {
      "id": "MO-ORACLE-01",
      "decision": "FIX",
      "severity": "P2 verification gap",
      "at": "2026-11-03T04:13:25.076032+00:00",
      "rationale": "Current14default-composition cases hold final getScope I/O across disposal, so post-await scope guard alone satisfies them. They do not independently qualify the distinct scope-return-to-mutation continuation window requiring the last prewrite guard. Add a real-service controlled-I/O notification ordered before its scope await; queue retirement after scope continuation but before mutation continuation, requiring zero old write and current replacement positive. No production guard replacement, elapsed-delay guess or current implementation defect claim. Preserve all14 and prior suites.",
